            <h4 data-number="5.2.7.4" id="subject-event"><span
            class="header-section-number">5.2.7.4</span> Subject
            Event</h4>
            <p><strong>Element name:</strong> &lt;<a
            href="https://lido-schema.org/schema/latest/lido.html#subjectEvent">lido:subjectEvent</a>&gt;</p>
            <p><strong>Note:</strong> Subject Event contains information
            about a particular event the object depicts or is about.
            Iconographical narratives and fictitious events are indexed
            as &lt;<a
            href="https://lido-schema.org/schema/latest/lido.html#subjectObject">lido:subjectObject</a>&gt;.</p>
            <p><strong>Example:</strong> Since there is no event as a
            topic in Leonardo’s <em>Mona Lisa</em>, a <a
            href="https://www.deutsche-digitale-bibliothek.de/item/34FHQ3ZRQMVVHPX3W63EGF5Q7I2MJDZ7">Punch
            cartoon</a> has been chosen as an example instead,
            addressing the theft of the <em>Mona Lisa</em> from the
            Louvre in 1911. The values for the preferred labels in
            English, German, and French are drawn from <a
            href="http://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q2727213">Wikidata</a>.
            Note that the LIDO <a
            href="http://terminology.lido-schema.org/lido00222">Event
            Type Terminology</a> does not provide terms for
            &lt;lido:subjectEvent&gt;. Rather, the event type should be
            drawn from an external vocabulary. Many authority files
            provide a generic concept as a broader term for named events
            that may be used as values for &lt;lido:eventType&gt;. In
            the following snippet, a superclass for the “<a
            href="https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q61266859">theft of Mona
            Lisa</a>” from Wikidata is used. The subject type is “<a
            href="http://terminology.lido-schema.org/lido00136">Identification</a>”.</p>
            <blockquote>
            <p><strong>Subject Event:</strong> Theft of Mona Lisa <br />
            <strong><em>Subject Type:</em></strong> Identification<br/>
            <strong>Event Type:</strong> theft
            <strong><em>Preference:</em></strong> Preferred</p>
            </blockquote>
            <div class="sourceCode" id="cb39"><pre
            class="sourceCode xml"><code class="sourceCode xml"><span id="cb39-1"><a href="#cb39-1" aria-hidden="true" tabindex="-1"></a>&lt;<span class="kw">lido:subjectSet</span>&gt;</span>
<span id="cb39-2"><a href="#cb39-2" aria-hidden="true" tabindex="-1"></a>    <span class="co">&lt;!-- Identification --&gt;</span></span>
<span id="cb39-3"><a href="#cb39-3" aria-hidden="true" tabindex="-1"></a>    &lt;<span class="kw">lido:subject</span></span>
<span id="cb39-4"><a href="#cb39-4" aria-hidden="true" tabindex="-1"></a><span class="ot">        lido:type=</span><span class="st">&quot;http://terminology.lido-schema.org/lido00136&quot;</span>&gt;</span>
<span id="cb39-5"><a href="#cb39-5" aria-hidden="true" tabindex="-1"></a>        &lt;<span class="kw">lido:subjectEvent</span>&gt;</span>
<span id="cb39-6"><a href="#cb39-6" aria-hidden="true" tabindex="-1"></a>            &lt;<span class="kw">lido:displayEvent</span></span>
<span id="cb39-7"><a href="#cb39-7" aria-hidden="true" tabindex="-1"></a><span class="ot">                xml:lang=</span><span class="st">&quot;en&quot;</span>&gt;</span>
<span id="cb39-8"><a href="#cb39-8" aria-hidden="true" tabindex="-1"></a>                Theft of Mona Lisa</span>
<span id="cb39-9"><a href="#cb39-9" aria-hidden="true" tabindex="-1"></a>            &lt;/<span class="kw">lido:displayEvent</span>&gt;</span>
<span id="cb39-10"><a href="#cb39-10" aria-hidden="true" tabindex="-1"></a>            &lt;<span class="kw">lido:event</span>&gt;</span>
<span id="cb39-11"><a h